# Copy to .env to enable GitHub sign-in when running the desktop app from
# source. Everything else works without this file.
#
# Nothing here is a secret: a client ID is public by design, and the proxy is a
# public endpoint. The OAuth client SECRET is deliberately absent — it lives in
# the Cloudflare Worker under proxy/, which is the whole reason that Worker
# exists: it exchanges the authorization code for a token so the desktop app
# never has to ship a secret it cannot keep.
#
# Without these two values the app still runs. `npm run dev`, the commit graph,
# staging, branches, merges, rebases and conflict resolution are all local git
# and need nothing. Only "Sign in with GitHub" — and what depends on it, so
# pull requests and "Share Patch as Link" — will fail. CI builds from a fork are
# in the same position, since GitHub passes no secrets to a fork's workflow run.
#
# To get your own pair (only needed if you are working ON sign-in):
#   1. https://github.com/settings/developers → New OAuth App
#      Authorization callback URL: gitgui://callback
#   2. Deploy proxy/ to Cloudflare Workers (`cd proxy && npx wrangler deploy`)
#      with the client secret set as a Worker secret, and point the URL below at
#      it.

VITE_GITHUB_CLIENT_ID=
VITE_GITHUB_PROXY_URL=
